Sending keys: ['cat > /app/output/answer.txt << \'EOF\'\n## Statute\n§3306(a)(2)(B)\n\n## Reasoning\nSection 3306(a)(2)(B) defines an "employer" for agricultural labor as any person who, on each of some 10 days during the calendar year or preceding calendar year, each day being in a different calendar week, employed at least 5 individuals in agricultural labor for some portion of the day.\n\nApplying the facts:\n- Jan 24: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred) - Week 4\n- Feb 4: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred) - Week 5\n- Mar 3: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred) - Week 9\n- Mar 18: 5 workers (Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George) - Week 11\n- Apr 1: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Fred, George) - Week 13\n- May 9: 5 workers (Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George) - Week 19\n- Oct 14: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, George) - Week 41\n- Oct 25: 6 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred, George) - Week 43\n- Nov 8: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Emily, Fred, George) - Week 45\n- Nov 22: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, Fred) - Week 47\n- Dec 1: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, George) - Week 48\n- Dec 2: 5 workers (Bob, Cameron, Dan, Emily, George) - Week 48\n\nAlice employed at least 5 individuals on 12 different days spanning 11 different calendar weeks. This satisfies the requirement of 10 days in different calendar weeks with at least 5 employees each.\n\nTherefore, Alice meets the definition of "employer" under §3306(a)(2)(B) for agricultural labor in 2017.\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: Entailment\nEOF\n'] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
