Sending keys: ["cat > /app/output/answer.txt <<'EOF'\n## Statute\n§1(a) - Tax imposed on married individuals filing joint returns\n§63(c)(2)(A) - Basic standard deduction for joint returns (200% of $3,000 = $6,000)\n§151(a), (b), (c) - Allowance of personal exemptions\n§151(d)(1) - Exemption amount of $2,000\n§152 - Dependent defined (Charlie qualifies as qualifying child)\n§7703(a)(1) - Marital status determined as of close of taxable year\n\n## Reasoning\n\n1. **Filing Status**: Alice and Bob are married (married Feb 3, 1992) and file jointly in 2013. Under §7703(a)(1), their marital status is determined as of the close of the taxable year.\n\n2. **Gross Income**: $71,879 (Alice) + $11,213 (Bob) = $83,092\n\n3. **Standard Deduction (§63)**: For a joint return, the basic standard deduction is 200% of $3,000 = $6,000. No additional standard deduction applies (no information about aged or blind status).\n\n4. **Personal Exemptions (§151)**: \n   - Alice (taxpayer): $2,000\n   - Bob (spouse): $2,000\n   - Charlie (dependent): $2,000\n   \n   Charlie qualifies as a dependent under §152 as a qualifying child (their child, born 2000, under age 19 in 2013, principal place of abode with them).\n   \n   Total exemptions: $6,000\n   \n   Phaseout under §151(d)(3) does not apply because AGI ($83,092) is below the §68(b) threshold of $300,000 for joint filers.\n\n5. **Taxable Income (§63)**: $83,092 - $6,000 (standard deduction) - $6,000 (exemptions) = $71,092\n\n6. **Tax Calculation (§1(a)(ii))**: Taxable income of $71,092 is over $36,900 but not over $89,150.\n   - Base tax: $5,535\n   - Plus 28% of excess over $36,900: ($71,092 - $36,900) × 0.28 = $34,192 × 0.28 = $9,573.76\n   - Total: $5,535 + $9,573.76 = $15,108.76\n\nRounded to nearest dollar: $15,109\n\n## Answer\nAnswer: 15109\nEOF\n"] min_timeout_sec: 0.5 max_timeout_sec: 180.0
